From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:04:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] presentation: panorama shapes learnt while scrolling wait for
 the grid to settle
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A browse fling through covers that have not been seen before commits each
tall ratio as soon as Coil reports it. The placeholder is 9/16, which is
wide, so the first tall commit bumped PanoramaMasonryContentEpoch while
the finger was still down. Each bump is a structural masonry relayout,
16-20 ms, and the frames dropped to 53-62% of animation ticks while new
covers loaded. Several Coil callbacks in one frame each wrote the epoch.

A first commit whose band differs from that placeholder now waits in
pendingCross until every panorama grid has settled, then one flush
commits them and bumps the epoch once. A first commit on the same side
of 0.75 still commits immediately and does not bump. When no grid is
scrolling, a first tall commit still commits in that flush.

Flushes are posted instead of run inline. The Android dispatcher posts
one main-looper message; further puts in that burst see flushQueued and
do not post again. Tests install a dispatcher whose post runs the block
immediately, or queues it, so the flush stays deterministic.

与 anikku-harmony 0025 / 0027 同一段代码，Anikku 侧待移植。
